 "text": "With so many books available, choosing the next one can be hard. I rely on a few simple methods. First, I ask friends what they enjoyed recently, and why. Next, I look at the first page in the shop before I decide. If the first page holds my attention, the rest usually will. Third, I mix different kinds of books. After a long novel, I often choose something short or something factual. Finally, I give myself permission to stop. If a book is not working for me after fifty pages, I put it aside without guilt. Reading should feel like a pleasure, so choose books that keep you turning the pages."
